      "title": "Implement Core Data Models and Database Schema",
      "description": "Design and implement the database schema and data models for the application, including session management, batch uploads, employee data, and scenario management.",
      "details": "1. Define SQLAlchemy models for:\n   - Session (sessions table)\n   - BatchUpload (batch_uploads table)\n   - EmployeeData (employee_data table)\n   - BatchScenario (batch_scenarios table)\n   - BatchCalculationResult (batch_calculation_results table)\n   - EmployeeCalculationResult (employee_calculation_results table)\n   - ImportTemplate (import_templates table)\n   - ScenarioAuditLog (scenario_audit_log table)\n2. Create Pydantic schemas for request/response validation\n3. Implement database access layer (DAL) classes for each model\n4. Set up Alembic migrations for initial schema creation\n5. Implement session management logic with anonymous sessions\n6. Configure data retention policies for temporary batch data\n\nExample Session model:\n```python\nclass Session(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"sessions\"\n    \n    id = Column(String, primary_key=True, index=True)\n    expires_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=False)\n    created_at = Column(DateTime, default=datetime.utcnow)\n    updated_at = Column(DateTime, default=datetime.utcnow, onupdate=datetime.utcnow)\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for each model and DAL class\n2. Integration tests for database operations\n3. Test session creation, expiration, and cleanup\n4. Verify data retention policies work as expected\n5. Test database migrations apply correctly\n6. Validate foreign key constraints and relationships",
