    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Implement Core Calculation Engine",
      "description": "Develop the core calculation engine that will be used across all modules (batch processing, individual calculator, and scenario playground) to ensure consistent bonus calculations.",
      "details": "1. Implement the core bonus formula: FinalBonus = BaseSalary × TargetBonusPct × (InvestmentWeight × InvestmentScoreMultiplier + QualitativeWeight × QualScoreMultiplier) × RAF\n2. Create pure functions for all intermediate calculations:\n   - Target bonus calculation\n   - Weighted performance scores\n   - RAF calculation with sensitivity and clamping\n   - Cap application logic (3x Base Salary and MRT Cap)\n3. Implement both backend (Python) and frontend (TypeScript) versions of the calculation engine\n4. Ensure calculation logic is identical between frontend and backend\n5. Create utility functions for validation and error handling\n\nExample calculation function:\n```python\ndef calculate_final_bonus(base_salary: float, target_bonus_pct: float, \n                         investment_weight: float, investment_score_multiplier: float,\n                         qualitative_weight: float, qual_score_multiplier: float,\n                         raf: float, is_mrt: bool = False, mrt_cap_pct: float = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the final bonus with all intermediate steps.\"\"\"\n    # Calculate target bonus\n    target_bonus = base_salary * target_bonus_pct\n    \n    # Calculate weighted performance\n    weighted_performance = (investment_weight * investment_score_multiplier + \n                           qualitative_weight * qual_score_multiplier)\n    \n    # Calculate pre-RAF bonus\n    pre_raf_bonus = target_bonus * weighted_performance\n    \n    # Apply RAF\n    initial_bonus = pre_raf_bonus * raf\n    \n    # Apply caps\n    base_salary_cap = base_salary * 3\n    mrt_cap = base_salary * mrt_cap_pct if is_mrt and mrt_cap_pct else float('inf')\n    \n    # Apply the lower of the caps if either is breached\n    final_bonus = min(initial_bonus, base_salary_cap, mrt_cap)\n    \n    return {\n        \"target_bonus\": target_bonus,\n        \"weighted_performance\": weighted_performance,\n        \"pre_raf_bonus\": pre_raf_bonus,\n        \"initial_bonus\": initial_bonus,\n        \"base_salary_cap\": base_salary_cap,\n        \"mrt_cap\": mrt_cap if is_mrt else None,\n        \"final_bonus\": final_bonus,\n        \"cap_applied\": \"3x_base\" if final_bonus == base_salary_cap and final_bonus < initial_bonus else\n                      \"mrt\" if final_bonus == mrt_cap and final_bonus < initial_bonus else None\n    }\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for all calculation functions using the truth table cases from Section 11\n2. Edge case tests using scenarios from Section 13\n3. Property-based testing to verify calculation invariants\n4. Cross-implementation tests to ensure frontend and backend calculations match\n5. Performance benchmarks for calculation speed\n6. Validation of RAF clamping behavior",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [
        2
      ],
      "status": "done",
