    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Implement Batch Processing Module - File Upload and Validation",
      "description": "Develop the file upload component of the Batch Processing Module, including CSV parsing, initial validation, and column preview functionality.",
      "details": "1. Create frontend components:\n   - BatchUploadContainer.tsx: Main container for the batch upload process\n   - FileUpload.tsx: Component for file selection and upload\n   - FilePreview.tsx: Display initial file preview and validation results\n2. Implement backend endpoints:\n   - POST /api/v1/batch/file: Upload CSV file\n   - GET /api/v1/batch/uploads/{upload_id}/columns: Get column info\n   - GET /api/v1/batch/uploads/template/{file_format}: Download template\n3. Implement file processing service:\n   - Parse CSV files\n   - Validate file structure and format\n   - Extract column headers and sample data\n   - Store raw file content in the database\n4. Add progress indicators for file upload\n5. Implement error handling for invalid files\n\nExample frontend component:\n```typescript\nconst FileUpload: React.FC = () => {\n  const [file, setFile] = useState<File | null>(null);\n  const [uploading, setUploading] = useState(false);\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  \n  const handleFileChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n    if (e.target.files && e.target.files.length > 0) {\n      setFile(e.target.files[0]);\n      setError(null);\n    }\n  };\n  \n  const handleUpload = async () => {\n    if (!file) return;\n    \n    setUploading(true);\n    setError(null);\n    \n    const formData = new FormData();\n    formData.append('file', file);\n    \n    try {\n      const response = await fetch('/api/v1/batch/file', {\n        method: 'POST',\n        body: formData,\n      });\n      \n      if (!response.ok) {\n        throw new Error('Upload failed');\n      }\n      \n      const data = await response.json();\n      // Handle successful upload\n    } catch (err) {\n      setError(err.message || 'An error occurred during upload');\n    } finally {\n      setUploading(false);\n    }\n  };\n  \n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4 border rounded-lg\">\n      <h2 className=\"text-xl font-bold mb-4\">Upload Employee Data</h2>\n      <input \n        type=\"file\" \n        accept=\".csv\" \n        onChange={handleFileChange} \n        className=\"mb-4\"\n      />\n      <button \n        onClick={handleUpload} \n        disabled={!file || uploading}\n        className=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded disabled:bg-gray-300\"\n      >\n        {uploading ? 'Uploading...' : 'Upload'}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p className=\"text-red-500 mt-2\">{error}</p>}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for file upload components\n2. Integration tests for file upload API endpoints\n3. Test with various CSV formats and sizes\n4. Validate error handling for malformed or invalid files\n5. Test file size limits and upload progress indicators\n6. Verify that column headers and sample data are correctly extracted",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "status": "done",
