    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Implement Batch Processing Module - Global Parameter Configuration",
      "description": "Develop the interface for configuring global calculation parameters to be applied to an entire batch.",
      "details": "1. Create frontend components:\n   - BatchParameterConfig.tsx: Form for configuring global calculation parameters\n2. Implement parameter configuration for:\n   - Standard Target Bonus %\n   - Investment & Qualitative Weights\n   - Parameters for Investment Score Multiplier curve\n   - Parameters for Qualitative Score Multiplier curve\n   - RAF calculation parameters or global RAF value\n   - MRT Cap Percentage and other policy settings\n3. Add validation for parameter values (e.g., weights must sum to 100%)\n4. Implement parameter storage in the batch upload record\n5. Create UI for parameter presets or quick configurations\n\nExample parameter configuration component:\n```typescript\nconst BatchParameterConfig: React.FC<{\n  onSubmit: (parameters: BatchParameters) => void;\n  initialValues?: BatchParameters;\n}> = ({ onSubmit, initialValues }) => {\n  const [parameters, setParameters] = useState<BatchParameters>(initialValues || {\n    targetBonusPct: 0.4, // 40%\n    investmentWeight: 0.6, // 60%\n    qualitativeWeight: 0.4, // 40%\n    rafSensitivity: 0.2,\n    rafLowerClamp: 0,\n    rafUpperClamp: 1.2,\n    mrtCapPct: 1.0, // 100% of base salary\n    useDirectRaf: true, // Use RAF from CSV if available\n  });\n  \n  const handleChange = (field: keyof BatchParameters, value: number | boolean) => {\n    setParameters(prev => ({\n      ...prev,\n      [field]: value\n    }));\n    \n    // If investment weight changes, adjust qualitative weight to maintain sum of 1\n    if (field === 'investmentWeight') {\n      setParameters(prev => ({\n        ...prev,\n        qualitativeWeight: 1 - Number(value)\n      }));\n    } else if (field === 'qualitativeWeight') {\n      setParameters(prev => ({\n        ...prev,\n        investmentWeight: 1 - Number(value)\n      }));\n    }\n  };\n  \n  const handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    onSubmit(parameters);\n  };\n  \n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className=\"p-4 border rounded-lg\">\n      <h2 className=\"text-xl font-bold mb-4\">Global Calculation Parameters</h2>\n      \n      <div className=\"mb-4\">\n        <label className=\"block mb-2\">Default Target Bonus %</label>\n        <input\n          type=\"number\"\n          min=\"0\"\n          max=\"2\"\n          step=\"0.01\"\n          value={parameters.targetBonusPct}\n          onChange={(e) => handleChange('targetBonusPct', Number(e.target.value))}\n          className=\"p-2 border rounded w-full\"\n        />\n      </div>\n      \n      <div className=\"mb-4\">\n        <label className=\"block mb-2\">Investment Weight</label>\n        <input\n          type=\"range\"\n          min=\"0\"\n          max=\"1\"\n          step=\"0.01\"\n          value={parameters.investmentWeight}\n          onChange={(e) => handleChange('investmentWeight', Number(e.target.value))}\n          className=\"w-full\"\n        />\n        <div className=\"flex justify-between\">\n          <span>0%</span>\n          <span>{(parameters.investmentWeight * 100).toFixed(0)}%</span>\n          <span>100%</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div className=\"mb-4\">\n        <label className=\"block mb-2\">Qualitative Weight</label>\n        <input\n          type=\"range\"\n          min=\"0\"\n          max=\"1\"\n          step=\"0.01\"\n          value={parameters.qualitativeWeight}\n          onChange={(e) => handleChange('qualitativeWeight', Number(e.target.value))}\n          className=\"w-full\"\n        />\n        <div className=\"flex justify-between\">\n          <span>0%</span>\n          <span>{(parameters.qualitativeWeight * 100).toFixed(0)}%</span>\n          <span>100%</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      {/* Additional parameter inputs... */}\n      \n      <button \n        type=\"submit\"\n        className=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded\"\n      >\n        Apply Parameters\n      </button>\n    </form>\n  );\n};\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for parameter configuration components\n2. Validation tests for parameter constraints (e.g., weights sum to 100%)\n3. Test parameter storage and retrieval\n4. Verify parameter application to batch calculations\n5. Test parameter presets and quick configurations\n6. Validate handling of parameter overrides from CSV data",
