      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Implement Batch Processing Module - Calculation and Results Display",
      "description": "Develop the batch calculation engine and results display interface for the Batch Processing Module.",
      "details": "1. Create frontend components:\n   - BatchResultsDisplay.tsx: Tabular display of batch calculation results\n   - BatchSummary.tsx: Summary statistics for the batch\n2. Implement backend endpoints:\n   - POST /api/v1/batch/uploads/{upload_id}/calculate_and_retrieve_results: Trigger calculation\n   - GET /api/v1/batch/uploads/{upload_id}/employees: Get processed employee data\n3. Implement batch calculation service:\n   - Process all valid employee records\n   - Apply global parameters and individual overrides\n   - Calculate bonuses using the core calculation engine\n   - Store results in the database\n4. Add sorting, filtering, and search functionality to the results table\n5. Implement export to CSV/Excel functionality\n6. Add progress tracking for large batch calculations\n\nExample batch calculation service:\n```python\nclass BatchCalculationService:\n    def __init__(self, db: Session):\n        self.db = db\n        self.calculation_engine = CalculationEngine()\n    \n    async def calculate_batch(self, batch_upload_id: int, global_parameters: dict) -> BatchCalculationResult:\n        \"\"\"Calculate bonuses for all employees in a batch.\"\"\"\n        # Get all employee data for this batch\n        employee_data = await EmployeeDataDAL(self.db).get_by_batch_upload_id(batch_upload_id)\n        \n        # Create a new batch scenario for this calculation\n        scenario = await BatchScenarioDAL(self.db).create(\n            session_id=employee_data[0].batch_upload.session_id if employee_data else None,\n            name=f\"Batch {batch_upload_id} - {datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')}\",\n            global_parameters=global_parameters,\n            is_saved=False\n        )\n        \n        # Create a new batch calculation result\n        batch_result = await BatchCalculationResultDAL(self.db).create(\n            scenario_id=scenario.id,\n            total_employees=len(employee_data),\n            total_bonus_pool=0,  # Will update after calculations\n            average_bonus=0,     # Will update after calculations\n            capped_employees=0   # Will update after calculations\n        )\n        \n        # Calculate bonus for each employee\n        employee_results = []\n        total_bonus = 0\n        capped_count = 0\n        \n        for employee in employee_data:\n            # Apply global parameters with potential individual overrides\n            params = self._merge_parameters(global_parameters, employee.parameter_overrides or {})\n            \n            # Calculate bonus\n            result = self.calculation_engine.calculate_final_bonus(\n                base_salary=employee.base_salary,\n                target_bonus_pct=employee.target_bonus_pct or params.get('targetBonusPct', 0),\n                investment_weight=employee.investment_weight or params.get('investmentWeight', 0.6),\n                investment_score_multiplier=employee.investment_score_multiplier,\n                qualitative_weight=employee.qualitative_weight or params.get('qualitativeWeight', 0.4),\n                qual_score_multiplier=employee.qual_score_multiplier,\n                raf=employee.raf,\n                is_mrt=employee.is_mrt,\n                mrt_cap_pct=employee.mrt_cap_pct or params.get('mrtCapPct')\n            )\n            \n            # Create employee calculation result\n            employee_result = await EmployeeCalculationResultDAL(self.db).create(\n                batch_result_id=batch_result.id,\n                employee_data_id=employee.id,\n                final_bonus=result['final_bonus'],\n                pre_raf_bonus=result['pre_raf_bonus'],\n                initial_bonus=result['initial_bonus'],\n                applied_cap=result['cap_applied']\n            )\n            \n            employee_results.append(employee_result)\n            total_bonus += result['final_bonus']\n            if result['cap_applied']:\n                capped_count += 1\n        \n        # Update batch result with summary statistics\n        average_bonus = total_bonus / len(employee_data) if employee_data else 0\n        await BatchCalculationResultDAL(self.db).update(\n            batch_result.id,\n            total_bonus_pool=total_bonus,\n            average_bonus=average_bonus,\n            capped_employees=capped_count\n        )\n        \n        return batch_result\n    \n    def _merge_parameters(self, global_params: dict, individual_overrides: dict) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Merge global parameters with individual overrides.\"\"\"\n        result = global_params.copy()\n        result.update(individual_overrides)\n        return result\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for batch calculation service\n2. Integration tests for batch calculation API endpoints\n3. Test with various batch sizes (small, medium, large)\n4. Validate summary statistics calculation\n5. Test sorting, filtering, and search functionality\n6. Verify export functionality produces correct CSV/Excel files\n7. Test progress tracking for large batches",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [
        3,
        6
      ],
      "status": "done",
