    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Implement Individual Compensation Calculator - Data Loading from Batch",
      "description": "Develop the functionality to load individual employee data from a processed batch into the Individual Compensation Calculator.",
      "details": "1. Create frontend components:\n   - CalculatorContainer.tsx: Main container for the individual calculator\n   - EmployeeSelector.tsx: Component for selecting an employee from batch results\n2. Implement navigation from batch results to individual calculator\n3. Create state management for individual calculator data\n4. Implement data loading from batch results to individual calculator\n5. Ensure global parameters from the batch are loaded as defaults\n\nExample employee selection component:\n```typescript\nconst EmployeeSelector: React.FC<{\n  batchId: number;\n  onEmployeeSelect: (employeeData: EmployeeData) => void;\n}> = ({ batchId, onEmployeeSelect }) => {\n  const [employees, setEmployees] = useState<EmployeeData[]>([]);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState('');\n  \n  useEffect(() => {\n    const fetchEmployees = async () => {\n      try {\n        setLoading(true);\n        const response = await fetch(`/api/v1/batch/uploads/${batchId}/employees`);\n        \n        if (!response.ok) {\n          throw new Error('Failed to fetch employees');\n        }\n        \n        const data = await response.json();\n        setEmployees(data);\n      } catch (err) {\n        setError(err.message || 'An error occurred');\n      } finally {\n        setLoading(false);\n      }\n    };\n    \n    fetchEmployees();\n  }, [batchId]);\n  \n  const filteredEmployees = employees.filter(emp => \n    emp.name?.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm.toLowerCase()) ||\n    emp.employee_id?.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm.toLowerCase())\n  );\n  \n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4 border rounded-lg\">\n      <h2 className=\"text-xl font-bold mb-4\">Select Employee</h2>\n      \n      <input\n        type=\"text\"\n        placeholder=\"Search by name or ID\"\n        value={searchTerm}\n        onChange={(e) => setSearchTerm(e.target.value)}\n        className=\"p-2 border rounded w-full mb-4\"\n      />\n      \n      {loading ? (\n        <p>Loading employees...</p>\n      ) : error ? (\n        <p className=\"text-red-500\">{error}</p>\n      ) : (\n        <div className=\"max-h-96 overflow-y-auto\">\n          <table className=\"w-full border-collapse\">\n            <thead>\n              <tr className=\"bg-gray-100\">\n                <th className=\"p-2 text-left\">ID</th>\n                <th className=\"p-2 text-left\">Name</th>\n                <th className=\"p-2 text-left\">Team</th>\n                <th className=\"p-2 text-left\">Base Salary</th>\n                <th className=\"p-2 text-left\">Actions</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n              {filteredEmployees.map(emp => (\n                <tr key={emp.id} className=\"border-t hover:bg-gray-50\">\n                  <td className=\"p-2\">{emp.employee_id}</td>\n                  <td className=\"p-2\">{emp.name}</td>\n                  <td className=\"p-2\">{emp.team}</td>\n                  <td className=\"p-2\">£{emp.base_salary.toLocaleString()}</td>\n                  <td className=\"p-2\">\n                    <button\n                      onClick={() => onEmployeeSelect(emp)}\n                      className=\"px-3 py-1 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded text-sm\"\n                    >\n                      Select\n                    </button>\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n              ))}\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for employee selection component\n2. Integration tests for navigation from batch results to individual calculator\n3. Test data loading from batch to individual calculator\n4. Verify global parameters are correctly loaded as defaults\n5. Test search and filtering functionality\n6. Validate handling of missing or incomplete employee data",
