    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Implement Scenario Playground Module - Scenario Management and Comparison",
      "description": "Develop the functionality to save, load, and compare scenarios in the Scenario Playground.",
      "details": "1. Create frontend components:\n   - ScenarioManager.tsx: Interface for saving and loading scenarios\n   - ScenarioComparison.tsx: Display for comparing scenarios\n2. Implement backend endpoints:\n   - PUT /api/v1/scenarios/{scenario_id}: Update a scenario\n   - POST /api/v1/scenarios/{scenario_id}/calculate: Recalculate results\n3. Create scenario saving and loading functionality\n4. Implement scenario comparison views\n5. Add scenario versioning or audit trails\n\nExample scenario manager component:\n```typescript\nconst ScenarioManager: React.FC<{\n  currentScenario: Scenario | null;\n  onSave: (name: string, description: string) => void;\n  onLoad: (scenarioId: number) => void;\n}> = ({ currentScenario, onSave, onLoad }) => {\n  const [scenarios, setScenarios] = useState<Scenario[]>([]);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [showSaveModal, setShowSaveModal] = useState(false);\n  const [scenarioName, setScenarioName] = useState('');\n  const [scenarioDescription, setScenarioDescription] = useState('');\n  \n  useEffect(() => {\n    const fetchScenarios = async () => {\n      try {\n        setLoading(true);\n        const response = await fetch('/api/v1/scenarios');\n        \n        if (!response.ok) {\n          throw new Error('Failed to fetch scenarios');\n        }\n        \n        const data = await response.json();\n        setScenarios(data.filter(scenario => scenario.is_saved));\n      } catch (err) {\n        setError(err.message || 'An error occurred');\n      } finally {\n        setLoading(false);\n      }\n    };\n    \n    fetchScenarios();\n  }, []);\n  \n  const handleSaveClick = () => {\n    setScenarioName(currentScenario?.name || '');\n    setScenarioDescription(currentScenario?.description || '');\n    setShowSaveModal(true);\n  };\n  \n  const handleSaveSubmit = () => {\n    onSave(scenarioName, scenarioDescription);\n    setShowSaveModal(false);\n  };\n  \n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4 border rounded-lg\">\n      <div className=\"flex justify-between items-center mb-4\">\n        <h2 className=\"text-xl font-bold\">Scenario Management</h2>\n        \n        <button\n          onClick={handleSaveClick}\n          className=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded\"\n          disabled={!currentScenario}\n        >\n          Save Current Scenario\n        </button>\n      </div>\n      \n      {loading ? (\n        <p>Loading scenarios...</p>\n      ) : error ? (\n        <p className=\"text-red-500\">{error}</p>\n      ) : (\n        <div>\n          <h3 className=\"font-bold mb-2\">Saved Scenarios</h3>\n          \n          {scenarios.length === 0 ? (\n            <p className=\"text-gray-500\">No saved scenarios</p>\n          ) : (\n            <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n              {scenarios.map(scenario => (\n                <div key={scenario.id} className=\"p-3 border rounded hover:bg-gray-50 cursor-pointer\"\n                     onClick={() => onLoad(scenario.id)}>\n                  <p className=\"font-medium\">{scenario.name}</p>\n                  {scenario.description && (\n                    <p className=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">{scenario.description}</p>\n                  )}\n                  <p className=\"text-sm text-gray-500\">\n                    Created: {new Date(scenario.created_at).toLocaleString()}\n                  </p>\n                </div>\n              ))}\n            </div>\n          )}\n        </div>\n      )}\n      \n      {/* Save Modal */}\n      {showSaveModal && (\n        <div className=\"fixed inset-0 bg-black bg-opacity-50 flex items-center justify-center z-50\">\n          <div className=\"bg-white p-6 rounded-lg w-full max-w-md\">\n            <h3 className=\"text-xl font-bold mb-4\">Save Scenario</h3>\n            \n            <div className=\"mb-4\">\n              <label className=\"block text-sm mb-1\">Scenario Name</label>\n              <input\n                type=\"text\"\n                value={scenarioName}\n                onChange={(e) => setScenarioName(e.target.value)}\n                className=\"p-2 border rounded w-full\"\n                required\n              />\n            </div>\n            \n            <div className=\"mb-4\">\n              <label className=\"block text-sm mb-1\">Description (Optional)</label>\n              <textarea\n                value={scenarioDescription}\n                onChange={(e) => setScenarioDescription(e.target.value)}\n                className=\"p-2 border rounded w-full h-24\"\n              />\n            </div>\n            \n            <div className=\"flex justify-end space-x-2\">\n              <button\n                onClick={() => setShowSaveModal(false)}\n                className=\"px-4 py-2 border rounded\"\n              >\n                Cancel\n              </button>\n              <button\n                onClick={handleSaveSubmit}\n                className=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded\"\n                disabled={!scenarioName}\n              >\n                Save\n              </button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for scenario management components\n2. Integration tests for scenario saving and loading\n3. Test scenario comparison functionality\n4. Verify scenario versioning and audit trails\n5. Test with multiple scenarios and large datasets\n6. Validate handling of scenario conflicts or errors",
      "priority": "medium",
      "dependencies": [
        12
      ],
      "status": "pending",
      "subtasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Implement Scenario Playground Module - Visualizations and Reporting",
      "description": "Develop the visualization and reporting components for the Scenario Playground.",
      "details": "1. Create frontend components:\n   - ScenarioVisualization.tsx: Charts and visualizations for scenario data\n   - ScenarioSummary.tsx: Summary statistics for the scenario\n   - ScenarioExport.tsx: Export functionality for scenario data\n2. Implement visualizations:\n   - Bonus distribution histograms\n   - Team-level aggregation charts\n   - Sensitivity analysis charts\n3. Create summary statistics display\n4. Implement export functionality for scenario data\n\nExample visualization component:\n```typescript\nimport { BarChart, Bar, XAxis, YAxis, CartesianGrid, Tooltip, Legend, ResponsiveContainer } from 'recharts';\n\nconst ScenarioVisualization: React.FC<{\n  scenarioResults: ScenarioResults;\n}> = ({ scenarioResults }) => {\n  // Prepare data for team-level aggregation chart\n  const teamData = Object.entries(scenarioResults.teamAggregations).map(([team, data]) => ({\n    team,\n    totalBonus: data.totalBonus,\n    averageBonus: data.averageBonus,\n    employeeCount: data.employeeCount\n  }));\n  \n  // Prepare data for bonus distribution histogram\n  const bonusRanges = [\n    '0-50k', '50k-100k', '100k-150k', '150k-200k', '200k-250k',\n    '250k-300k', '300k-350k', '350k-400k', '400k-450k', '450k-500k', '500k+'\n  ];\n  \n  const distributionData = bonusRanges.map(range => {\n    const count = scenarioResults.bonusDistribution[range] || 0;\n    return { range, count };\n  });\n  \n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4 border rounded-lg\">\n      <h2 className=\"text-xl font-bold mb-4\">Scenario Visualizations</h2>\n      \n      <div className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h3 className=\"font-bold mb-2\">Team Aggregations</h3>\n        <div className=\"h-80\">\n          <ResponsiveContainer width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n            <BarChart data={teamData}>\n              <CartesianGrid strokeDasharray=\"3 3\" />\n              <XAxis dataKey=\"team\" />\n              <YAxis yAxisId=\"left\" orientation=\"left\" stroke=\"#8884d8\" />\n              <YAxis yAxisId=\"right\" orientation=\"right\" stroke=\"#82ca9d\" />\n              <Tooltip />\n              <Legend />\n              <Bar yAxisId=\"left\" dataKey=\"totalBonus\" name=\"Total Bonus (£)\" fill=\"#8884d8\" />\n              <Bar yAxisId=\"right\" dataKey=\"averageBonus\" name=\"Average Bonus (£)\" fill=\"#82ca9d\" />\n            </BarChart>\n          </ResponsiveContainer>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h3 className=\"font-bold mb-2\">Bonus Distribution</h3>\n        <div className=\"h-80\">\n          <ResponsiveContainer width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n            <BarChart data={distributionData}>\n              <CartesianGrid strokeDasharray=\"3 3\" />\n              <XAxis dataKey=\"range\" />\n              <YAxis />\n              <Tooltip />\n              <Legend />\n              <Bar dataKey=\"count\" name=\"Number of Employees\" fill=\"#8884d8\" />\n            </BarChart>\n          </ResponsiveContainer>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h3 className=\"font-bold mb-2\">Summary Statistics</h3>\n        <div className=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n          <div className=\"p-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg text-center\">\n            <h4 className=\"text-sm font-bold mb-1\">Total Bonus Pool</h4>\n            <p className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-blue-700\">£{scenarioResults.totalBonusPool.toLocaleString()}</p>\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"p-4 bg-green-50 rounded-lg text-center\">\n            <h4 className=\"text-sm font-bold mb-1\">Average Bonus</h4>\n            <p className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-green-700\">£{scenarioResults.averageBonus.toLocaleString()}</p>\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"p-4 bg-yellow-50 rounded-lg text-center\">\n            <h4 className=\"text-sm font-bold mb-1\">Capped Employees</h4>\n            <p className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-yellow-700\">{scenarioResults.cappedEmployees} / {scenarioResults.totalEmployees}</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div>\n        <button \n          onClick={() => {\n            // Export logic here\n            const csvContent = `Team,Total Bonus,Average Bonus,Employee Count\\n` +\n                            teamData.map(team => \n                              `${team.team},${team.totalBonus},${team.averageBonus},${team.employeeCount}`\n                            ).join('\\n');\n            \n            const blob = new Blob([csvContent], { type: 'text/csv;charset=utf-8;' });\n            const link = document.createElement('a');\n            const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n            link.setAttribute('href', url);\n            link.setAttribute('download', 'scenario_results.csv');\n            link.style.visibility = 'hidden';\n            document.body.appendChild(link);\n            link.click();\n            document.body.removeChild(link);\n          }}\n          className=\"px-4 py-2 bg-green-500 text-white rounded\"\n        >\n          Export Results\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for visualization components\n2. Verify chart data is correctly derived from scenario results\n3. Test summary statistics calculation\n4. Validate export functionality produces correct files\n5. Test with various dataset sizes and distributions\n6. Verify visualizations are responsive and render correctly on different screen sizes",
      "priority": "medium",
      "dependencies": [
        13
      ],
      "status": "pending",
      "subtasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Implement Session Management and Application Workflow",
      "description": "Develop the session management system and implement the overall application workflow as specified in FR0.",
      "details": "1. Create frontend components:\n   - AppLayout.tsx: Main application layout with navigation\n   - LandingPage.tsx: Default landing page (Batch Upload interface)\n   - SessionManager.tsx: Component for managing the user session\n2. Implement backend endpoints:\n   - POST /api/v1/batch/sessions: Create a new anonymous session\n   - GET /api/v1/batch/sessions/current: Get current session details\n3. Create session management logic:\n   - Generate and store anonymous session IDs\n   - Associate uploaded data with sessions\n   - Implement session expiration and cleanup\n4. Implement the overall application workflow:\n   - Landing Page -> Batch Upload -> Column Mapping -> Parameter Configuration -> Batch Results\n   - Batch Results -> Individual Calculator\n   - Batch Results/Individual Calculator -> Scenario Playground\n5. Add navigation between modules\n6. Implement data retention policies\n\nExample session management service:\n```python\nclass SessionService:\n    def __init__(self, db: Session):\n        self.db = db\n    \n    async def create_session(self) -> SessionModel:\n        \"\"\"Create a new anonymous session.\"\"\"\n        # Generate a secure random session ID\n        session_id = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n        \n        # Set expiration time (e.g., 24 hours from now)\n        expires_at = datetime.utcnow() + timedelta(hours=24)\n        \n        # Create session in database\n        session = await SessionDAL(self.db).create(\n            id=session_id,\n            expires_at=expires_at\n        )\n        \n        return session\n    \n    async def get_session(self, session_id: str) -> Optional[SessionModel]:\n        \"\"\"Get a session by ID.\"\"\"\n        session = await SessionDAL(self.db).get_by_id(session_id)\n        \n        if not session:\n            return None\n        \n        # Check if session has expired\n        if session.expires_at < datetime.utcnow():\n            await self.cleanup_session(session_id)\n            return None\n        \n        return session\n    \n    async def extend_session(self, session_id: str) -> Optional[SessionModel]:\n        \"\"\"Extend the expiration time of a session.\"\"\"\n        session = await self.get_session(session_id)\n        \n        if not session:\n            return None\n        \n        # Extend expiration time\n        new_expires_at = datetime.utcnow() + timedelta(hours=24)\n        \n        # Update session in database\n        updated_session = await SessionDAL(self.db).update(\n            session_id,\n            expires_at=new_expires_at\n        )\n        \n        return updated_session\n    \n    async def cleanup_session(self, session_id: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Clean up all data associated with a session.\"\"\"\n        # Delete all batch uploads associated with this session\n        batch_uploads = await BatchUploadDAL(self.db).get_by_session_id(session_id)\n        \n        for batch_upload in batch_uploads:\n            # Delete employee data associated with this batch upload\n            await EmployeeDataDAL(self.db).delete_by_batch_upload_id(batch_upload.id)\n            \n            # Delete the batch upload itself\n            await BatchUploadDAL(self.db).delete(batch_upload.id)\n        \n        # Delete all scenarios associated with this session\n        scenarios = await BatchScenarioDAL(self.db).get_by_session_id(session_id)\n        \n        for scenario in scenarios:\n            # Delete calculation results associated with this scenario\n            batch_results = await BatchCalculationResultDAL(self.db).get_by_scenario_id(scenario.id)\n            \n            for batch_result in batch_results:\n                await EmployeeCalculationResultDAL(self.db).delete_by_batch_result_id(batch_result.id)\n                await BatchCalculationResultDAL(self.db).delete(batch_result.id)\n            \n            # Delete the scenario itself\n            await BatchScenarioDAL(self.db).delete(scenario.id)\n        \n        # Delete all templates associated with this session\n        await ImportTemplateDAL(self.db).delete_by_session_id(session_id)\n        \n        # Finally, delete the session itself\n        await SessionDAL(self.db).delete(session_id)\n```",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit tests for session management components and services\n2. Integration tests for session API endpoints\n3. Test session creation, expiration, and cleanup\n4. Verify data retention policies work as expected\n5. Test the overall application workflow\n6. Validate navigation between modules\n7. Test with multiple concurrent sessions",
